# Platformer_Controls.events — the reusable platformer movement keys (Task 36 Part G).
#
# The input half of the platformer controller, written once and pulled into a sheet with
# `include "Platformer_Controls"` — the same split `FPS_Controls.events` makes. What stays in the
# including sheet is what belongs to a game's design rather than to a controller: the ladder grab,
# the poses, the checkpoint and the death/respawn. (Gravity, collide-and-slide walking and the
# ground probe already live in shared C#: `PhysicsMovement`, `CharacterStep`.)
#
# What the including sheet provides:
#   · `my WalkSpeed` — walk speed in cm/s. Unset means every move runs at 0, so set it on start.
#   · `my JumpPower` — take-off speed in cm/s (the default `jump` is 350 when the sheet says
#     nothing, which is why this line names the variable).
#   · its ladder grab on W ABOVE the include line if it has one: events run top to bottom, and
#     `climb` registers the climb immediately, so this file's `unless me is climbing` sees it in
#     the same tick and the walk does not fight the ascent.
#
# Setup (editor): a CharacterController on the actor, its EventSheet ticked *Use Physics Movement*
# (and *Configure Character Body* for the shipped capsule). The ground probe uses the sheet's
# Ground Check Distance — 10 cm by default — and a sheet at 0 always reads airborne.
#
# Keys: W walks, Space jumps when grounded.

# --- walking ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `unless me is climbing` is what lets a sheet own W for a ladder (or any other mode) without the
# walk running underneath it.
when W is held
  unless me is climbing
  move forward speed my WalkSpeed

# --- jumping ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `jump` refuses a mid-air take-off on its own; the gate makes that visible, and it is also what
# keeps a sheet's `Jump` clip from restarting on every held tick.
when Space is pressed
  unless me is airborne
  jump strength my JumpPower
